## Why This Is Asked

This question tests practical risk reduction for credential leakage in automated data exports, ensuring tenants are isolated and tokens are short-lived with clear containment procedures.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant least privilege with STS AssumeRole
- Short-lived credentials and rotation
- Secrets management and tenant-scoped IAM policies
- CloudTrail/GuardDuty for anomaly detection
- IR playbook with containment and recovery steps

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: AssumeRole for a tenant export job using AWS SDK v3
const { STSClient, AssumeRoleCommand } = require("@aws-sdk/client-sts");
const sts = new STSClient({ region: "us-east-1" });
const cmd = new AssumeRoleCommand({
  RoleArn: tenantRoleArn,
  RoleSessionName: "export-tenant-"+tenantId,
  DurationSeconds: 900
});
const resp = await sts.send(cmd);
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test the mitigation against token replay?
- What metrics would indicate token misuse?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests your ability to apply fundamental security controls to third-party components—a common real-world risk at many companies. It evaluates your understanding of vendor vetting, data minimization, privacy controls, and incident response readiness.

## Key Concepts
- Third-party risk management
- Data minimization and PII redaction
- User consent and privacy controls
- Observability and incident response readiness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: redact PII from analytics payload
function redact(payload) {
  const redacted = { ...payload };
  if (redacted.userEmail) redacted.userEmail = "[REDACTED]";
  if (redacted.userPhone) redacted.userPhone = "[REDACTED]";
  return redacted;
}

// Example: hash identifiers before transmission
function hashIdentifier(identifier) {
  return crypto.createHash('sha256').update(identifier).digest('hex');
}
```

